    "final_answer": "I have all the information I need. Let me provide the final answer.\n\n## Final Answer\n\nI found a suitable Intermediate-level course on Coursera about Blockchain Technology that matches all the criteria:\n\n### Course: **Smart Contracts (智能合约)**\n- **URL:** https://www.coursera.org/learn/smarter-contracts\n\n### Key Details:\n- **Provider Institution:** University at Buffalo (part of SUNY — State University of New York, a well-known public research university)\n- **Instructor:** **Bina Ramamurthy**\n- **Level:** Intermediate (中级)\n- **Duration:** Approximately 2 weeks at 10 hours per week (within the 1-4 weeks range)\n- **Number of Modules:** 4 modules\n- **Rating:** 4.6 stars (based on 2,338 reviews)\n- **Enrollment:** 81,111 students already enrolled\n- **Next Start Date:** September 25\n- **Language:** English (with 23 translations available, including Chinese)\n\n### Main Goals of the Course:\nAccording to the course description: *\"This is the second course in the Blockchain specialization and will help you design, code, deploy, and execute smart contracts.\"*\n\nSpecifically, you will learn to:\n- **Design and write smart contracts** using the **Solidity** programming language\n- **Test and deploy smart contracts** in the **Remix development environment**\n- Build foundational skills in **software design, cryptographic protocols, validation, solution design, event-driven programming, business logic, application deployment, and blockchain transactions**\n\nThis course is part of the broader **Blockchain Specialization** offered by University at Buffalo, making it a natural fit for those looking to deepen their knowledge of blockchain technology in a structured, academically backed format.",
